course: dictionary
lesson: 9432
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the sentence to tell you which one is meant. «The stag lifted its head and looked across the valley.» The clues are the valley and the head lifted high, so a stag here is an animal: an adult male deer with large branching antlers.
explain: «Her brother's stag party is next Saturday.» Now the clues are party and wedding, so stag means something different: a party for a man just before his wedding, with only his male friends. The same word, a different meaning, because the words around it are different.
explain: Stag also appears in longer names, like «stag beetle». The male stag beetle's huge jaws look like a deer's antlers, so the word is a clue to what the beetle looks like. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: A stag is an adult male deer, usually with large branching antlers.
fact: A stag party or stag night is a party for a man just before his wedding, with only his male friends. It is mostly used in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: A female deer is called a doe or a hind, and a young deer is called a fawn.
fact: Stags grow new antlers every year, so the number of points can change from year to year.
fact: Each tip of an antler is called a point or tine, but points do not show a stag's exact age.
exercise: «The stag stood still at the edge of the wood.» What is a stag here? | *An adult male deer with large antlers | A bird with long legs | A kind of tree | A young deer
exercise: Ella reads, «Tom's stag party is on Friday, with only his mates.» What is a stag party? | A party for every guest at a wedding | *A party for a man just before his wedding, with only his male friends | A school sports day | A quiet picnic in the park
exercise: Which word in the lessons names the female deer? | *doe | fawn | stag | antler
test: «The male stag beetle's huge jaws look like a deer's antlers.» What does stag beetle name? | *A big beetle whose jaws look like antlers | A deer that is also a beetle | A fast beetle that runs in races | A beetle that lives only in London
test: «Each tip of an antler is called a point, and a big red deer stag can have twelve or more.» What is a point? | *A tip of an antler | A type of stag party | A pointed hoof | A tail of a deer
exam: Jayden reads, «In autumn the stags roared and fought, so keepers asked people to stay 50 metres away.» Which meaning of stag fits best? | Stags are birds that sing in autumn | Stags are young deer that stay close to their mothers | *Stags are adult male deer, and in autumn they roar and fight | Stags are small beetles that live in rotting wood
